      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have some concerns about the playback APIs growing incrementally for each new usecase like this: right now we want to play frames, but in the future we\u0027ll want to play partial frames etc. In the JS debugger prototype (and in GAPID and likely others) there is a concept of a point until which to replay, and the API work in terms of these replay points.\n\nSo `Play()` is `PlayUntil(GetLastCommandPoint())` and `PlayFrame()` is `PlayUntil(GetPresentCommandPoints()[i++])`.\n\nWe don\u0027t need to do this *right now* because we just want to reach a limited milestone, but let file a new issue and add a TODO with information about how we\u0027d rework the API to be more useful in the future.",
      "revId": "12cf0060876e5414b02030bc70ae87138576cefb",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
